27	/// How Typst overrides the [MathML Core User Agent Stylesheet][UA].
28	///
29	/// What follows are explanations justifying the inclusion of each rule. The
30	/// main purpose is to ensure the MathML produced is rendered by browsers as
31	/// closely as possible to Typst's paged export. Things not included here mean
32	/// that the UA stylesheet already matches!
33	///
34	/// The oracle of truth for Typst's paged export are the styles applied in the
35	/// [`resolve_*` functions in `typst_library::math::ir::resolve`][resolve].
36	/// These styles are the [`style_*` functions in `typst_library::math`][style].
37	/// Their documentation includes how they map to CSS properties in MathML Core.
38	///
39	/// # Alignment
40	///
41	/// To get the alternating alignment working, we use the `justify-items` and
42	/// `text-align` properties on `mtd`. In the future,
43	/// [`justify-items`][alignment] should work across all browsers. For now, only
44	/// Chromium support this. So we put `text-align` after to accommodate other
45	/// browsers.
46	///
47	/// Inline multiline equations and the `cases` class on an `mtable` are always
48	/// left aligned. The `aligned` class on an `mtable` alternates right-left
49	/// alignment. Finally the `right-align` and `left-align` classes can be used
50	/// on either an `mtable` or an `mtd` to provide right and left alignment,
51	/// respectively.
52	///
53	/// The `cases` and `aligned` classes on `mtable` all have the horizontal
54	/// spacing (padding) set to zero. We also have the `flushed`, `left-flush` and
55	/// `right-flush` classes for `mtd` that set the corresponding horizontal
56	/// spacing to zero.
57	///
58	/// # Tables
59	///
60	/// The UA stylesheet sets `math-style: compact` at the top-level for every
61	/// `mtable`. We undo this, and instead set on `mtd` the properties matching
62	/// [`style_for_denominator`][denom].
63	///
64	/// # Equations
65	///
66	/// For equations we are using `mtable` to do multiline layout and alignment.
67	/// So we undo all changes to the CSS math properties, and set the padding to
68	/// zero so that there is no space between columns.
69	///
70	/// To ensure that there is some line spacing between each line in a multiline
71	/// equation, we set bottom padding only for all but the last row of `mtd`.
72	///
73	/// # Fractions
74	///
75	/// The UA stylesheet adds a fixed inline padding of `1px`. This, however, is
76	/// added within the denominator and numerator, making the fraction rule longer
77	/// instead of being added around the fraction. We use `margin-inline` to fix
78	/// this and use the same value of `0.1em` as in paged export.
79	///
80	/// # Accents
81	///
82	/// We enable by default the `dtls` OpenType feature for all top accents, and
83	/// then add a class to explicitly disable this.
84	///
85	/// # Other rules for scriptlevel, displaystyle and math-shift
86	///
87	/// The first set of rules ensure bottom attachements are [cramped], matching
88	/// bottom-left and bottom-right ones.
89	///
90	/// The second set of rules undo the UA stylesheet's and our immediately prior
91	/// rules on accents themselves.
92	///
93	/// [UA]: https://www.w3.org/TR/mathml-core/#user-agent-stylesheet
94	/// [resolve]: typst_library::math::ir#functions
95	/// [style]: typst_library::math#functions
96	/// [denom]: typst_library::math::style_for_denominator
97	/// [alignment]: https://github.com/w3c/mathml-core/issues/156
98	/// [cramped]: typst_library::math::style_cramped
99	pub(crate) static EQUATION_CSS_STYLES: LazyLock<EcoString> = LazyLock::new(|| {
100	    eco_format!(
101	        "\
102	/* Alignment */
103	mtable.{RIGHT_ALIGN_CLASS} mtd,
104	mtable mtd.{RIGHT_ALIGN_CLASS},
105	mtable.{LEFT_ALIGN_CLASS} mtd.{RIGHT_ALIGN_CLASS},
106	mtable.{ALIGNED_CLASS} mtd:nth-child(odd) {{
107	  justify-items: end;
108	  text-align: right;
109	}}
110	mtable.{CASES_CLASS} mtd,
111	mtable.{LEFT_ALIGN_CLASS} mtd,
112	mtable mtd.{LEFT_ALIGN_CLASS},
113	mtable.{ALIGNED_CLASS} mtd:nth-child(even),
114	math:is(:not([display])) > mtable.{MULTILINE_EQUATION_CLASS} mtd {{
115	  justify-items: start;
116	  text-align: left;
117	}}
118	mtable.{CASES_CLASS} mtd,
119	mtable.{ALIGNED_CLASS} mtd,
120	mtable mtd.{FLUSHED_CLASS},
121	mtable mtd.{LEFT_FLUSH_CLASS} {{
122	  padding-left: 0;
123	}}
124	mtable.{CASES_CLASS} mtd,
125	mtable.{ALIGNED_CLASS} mtd,
126	mtable mtd.{FLUSHED_CLASS},
127	mtable mtd.{RIGHT_FLUSH_CLASS} {{
128	  padding-right: 0;
129	}}
130	
131	/* Tables */
132	mtable {{
133	  math-style: inherit;
134	}}
135	mtd {{
136	  math-depth: auto-add;
137	  math-style: compact;
138	  math-shift: compact;
139	}}
140	
141	/* Equations */
142	mtable.{MULTILINE_EQUATION_CLASS} mtd {{
143	  math-depth: inherit;
144	  math-style: inherit;
145	  math-shift: inherit;
146	  padding: 0;
147	}}
148	math > mtable.{MULTILINE_EQUATION_CLASS} mtr:not(:last-child) mtd {{
149	  padding-bottom: {};
150	}}
151	
152	/* Fractions */
153	mfrac {{
154	  padding-inline: 0;
155	  margin-inline: {};
156	}}
157	
158	/* Accents */
159	mover[accent=\"true\" i] > :first-child {{
160	  font-feature-settings: \"dtls\";
161	}}
162	mover.dotted[accent=\"true\" i] > :first-child {{
163	  font-feature-settings: \"dtls\" 0;
164	}}
165	
166	/* Other rules for scriptlevel, displaystyle and math-shift */
167	munder > :nth-child(2),
168	munderover > :nth-child(2) {{
169	  math-shift: compact
170	}}
171	munder[accentunder=\"true\" i] > :not(:first-child),
172	mover[accent=\"true\" i] > :not(:first-child) {{
173	  math-depth: inherit;
174	  math-style: inherit;
175	  math-shift: inherit;
176	}}",
177	        EQUATION_ROW_GAP.to_css(()),
178	        FRAC_PADDING.to_css(())
179	    )
180	});
